cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Seismic Descent: Global Optimization via Spatially Correlated Landscape Deformation"
authors:
  - family-names: "Carbonell"
    given-names: "Mario R."
version: 0.24.1
date-released: 2026-10-03
repository-code: "https://github.com/mcarbonell/seismic-descent"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - global optimization
  - random fourier features
  - landscape deformation
  - correlated noise
  - derivative-based optimization
abstract: >-
  Seismic Descent is a global optimization algorithm that perturbs the
  objective landscape with a time-varying, spatially correlated random
  field (RFF/ORF/Lissajous), letting plain gradient descent escape
  local minima while tracking the best point against the unperturbed
  objective.
